add(81,'unproved claim','161-5',[28,29],'1454-1486','Si on a une telle section','Given an extension1→A→E→Γ→1 and one splitting α, every other splitting is z(γ)α(γ) for a1-cocycle for the α-conjugation action. This does not prove splitting existence.','Statement remains valid independently of whether the final question on029 is cancelled.','agrees','The conditional language is explicit on028.')
add(82,'idea of the earlier run','161-5',[28,29],'1470-1495','φ(π)={e}','For any subgroup π⊂Γ, the neutral fibre of H¹(Γ,A)→H¹(π,A) equals normalized cocycles z|π=1 modulo A^π. It parametrizes extensions of a fixed partial splitting, once an extension exists.','No normality is needed for this normalized-cocycle description.','agrees','Proof is normalization by a coboundary; conjugators preserving normalization lie in A^π.')
add(83,'reading question','161-5',[29],'1489-1495','injectif ... noyau nul','Trivial neutral fibre of nonabelian H¹ restriction is weaker than full injectivity; all fibres require the analogous statement for twisted coefficient actions.','The manuscript’s abbreviation is uncertain; the stronger/weaker mathematical distinction is exact.','agrees','The parenthesis explicitly weakens injectivity; Codex marks the larger block deleted, so historical live status is unresolved.')
add(84,'idea of the earlier run','161-5',[27,29],'1438-1441,1480-1495','π⊂Γ','Only with π normal can normalized cocycles descend to Γ/π with coefficients A^π. For a general subgroup use SA23-282.','A necessary hypothesis check, not a new original quotient-group assertion.','agrees','The page supplies no normality for the separately named subgroup.')
add(85,'withdrawn in the same text','161-5',[29],'1496-1498','torseur[deleted] ... esp. homogène','If the extensions form one A^π-orbit, its stabilizer is A^Γ, so the orbit need not be a torsor.','Local word replacement is clear; whether the whole paragraph is subsequently deleted is a separate unresolved witness conflict.','understates','The note correctly explains the stabilizer but omits Codex’s larger deletion scope.','corrected')
add(86,'idea of the earlier run','161-5',[27,28,29],'1438-1498','Est-il vrai ... conjugués','For the explicit model K=Qp,G=Gm,ρ=j=1,A=Ω×,Γ=π×Z acting through π on Ω, extension multipliers are b∈Qp× and conjugation by A^π is trivial. Thus uniqueness fails.','Model is Hua’s reconstruction; the manuscript’s Γ remains unspecified.','agrees','This refutes the unrestricted model, not a fully fixed original admissible-period problem.')
